          "Lead with housing affordability and rental-market stabilization as the primary legislative priority: at 80.7% renter-occupied and $42,647 median income, the typical household is spending 35-45% of gross income on rent, and housing cost burden is the most direct material pressure on household economic security. A legislative record of wins in rent stabilization, tenant protection, housing trust fund expansion, or development of permanently affordable units is the most concrete proof of responsive representation.",
          "Engage the 75% communities-of-color constituency with legislative focus on healthcare access, maternal health equity, and economic mobility pathways: with only 25.6% college attainment and a 34.0 median age, this district has a large population of young adults and families whose economic futures depend on job training, wage growth, and access to healthcare and childcare. Demonstrate legislative effectiveness on these material concerns rather than abstract party positioning.",
          "Use unopposed status to build legislative depth, not to reduce constituent engagement: unopposed elections create a strategic trap where incumbents become less responsive precisely when they face no electoral pressure, which erodes the active relationship with voters that prevents credible challengers from emerging. Treat the unopposed result as opportunity to deepen constituent service, not permission to manage on autopilot.",
