          { name: "Partisan Framing Over Constituency Material Needs", tag: "avoid", why: "CT-HD-10's 69% Democratic margin reflects real economic and demographic characteristics — working-class Hispanic/Latino plurality, significant Black/African American community, high renter rate, low college attainment — that are deeply material to households' daily lives. A campaign that relies on abstract Democratic messaging or tribal in-group signaling rather than specific answers to questions about wage growth, housing cost, healthcare access, and job quality will find that the margin is softer than it appears. The constituency voted Democratic because they see it as responsive to their economic interests; any campaign that abandons that material focus for partisan positioning will hand an opportunity to an opponent with concrete solutions." }
