          { name: "Partisan Ideology as a Substitute for Governance Competence", tag: "avoid", why: "CT-HD-14 is not a district where ideological messaging or partisan appeals will move voters; it is a district of educated professionals who evaluate candidates on specific competence in education, fiscal management, and infrastructure quality. Any candidate — Republican or Democratic — who leads with partisan rhetoric rather than concrete governance proposals is misreading the constituency and will lose persuadable voters to a more competent alternative." },
          { name: "Taking the Affluent Homeowner Majority for Granted", tag: "avoid", why: "A 55-45 margin is not a safe majority; it is a vulnerable plurality in a district where 45% of voters actively chose someone else and where affluent professionals are accustomed to holding elected officials accountable for specific performance. Any candidate who campaigns as though 55% represents a comfortable hold — rather than engaging the opposition's concerns about education quality, fiscal management, or specific governance failures — is arithmetically vulnerable to a credible challenger who presents as more competent." }
