          "Engage the 40.1% college-educated constituency on institutional quality and professional advancement: university partnerships, healthcare infrastructure, and the quality of professional services and opportunity in the district are concrete issues where visible Democratic investment strengthens the seat.",
          "Attend to the 29.5% renter population—younger professionals and working families—with specific messaging on housing affordability, rental stability, and economic mobility; this population can drift to alternative candidates if they perceive Democratic governance as addressing only homeowner interests.",
          "Recognize that 81% is a supermajority result, not a ceiling: in a district this Democratic and this affluent, the strategic vulnerability is complacency or perceived underperformance on specific constituent concerns, not partisan competition—active engagement with community institutions (churches, civic organizations, professional networks) is the primary retention strategy."
