          "Engage the renter and minority communities with specific equity focus: the 18.9% renter rate and meaningful Hispanic, Asian, and Black populations deserve constituent attention around housing policy, school resource equity, and economic mobility pathways rather than being absorbed into the affluent homeowner narrative.",
          "Recognize that unopposed status is not a governance mandate: the 2024 lack of opposition reflects Democratic resource allocation, not consensus; any candidate in 2026 or beyond who contests this seat on competence, education quality, or healthcare affordability can compete effectively if the incumbent has not built active constituent relationships and demonstrated problem-solving on the concerns that matter most to different parts of the district."
