          { name: "Treating the District's High Income & Education as Guarantees of Republican Support", tag: "avoid", why: "Affluent, college-educated suburban districts have become significantly more competitive nationally over the past decade precisely because professional-class voters increasingly evaluate on specific governance delivery rather than partisan default. At 53-47 in a district this affluent and educated, assuming that income and education alone will hold Republican voters is strategically dangerous; this is a constituency that has demonstrated willingness to vote opposition when they believe their governance concerns are not being addressed. Complacency about this margin in a professional-class suburb will produce erosion, not consolidation." }
