          "Lead with property tax and school funding: the 86.7% homeowner rate and 46.3% college attainment signal a constituency intensely focused on school quality and whether rising property taxes are justified by school performance; this is the primary fiscal anxiety in affluent suburbia and the most concrete ground on which to build voter preference.",
          "Engage healthcare cost control and access specifically: at $118k+ income and 50.8 median age, voters are managing both employer-sponsored healthcare and aging-parent care concerns; state policies on healthcare provider network adequacy, prescription drug costs, and long-term care planning are direct household budget issues that differentiate candidates in this demographic.",
          "Build credibility on infrastructure and municipal service delivery: affluent suburbs evaluate heavily on whether roads are maintained, traffic is managed, and municipal services function without visible waste; this is the everyday governance competence that persuadable voters in CT-HD-35 use to evaluate candidates, not abstract ideology."
