          { name: "Treating 63% as Unassailable or Taking the Constituency for Granted", tag: "avoid", why: "While 63% is a comfortable margin, it is not a landslide in a prosperous suburban district where voters actively evaluate on governance competence. An incumbent who becomes inattentive to constituent service, allows municipal service quality to decline, or allows a challenger to outmaneuver on fiscal credibility risks watching a safe district inch toward competitiveness. The 37% opposition is smaller, but it is not immobilized; it will grow if it has a credible alternative and the incumbent stops delivering." }
