          "Invest visibly in constituent service and local problem-solving: affluent, educated, low-renter districts reward representatives who demonstrate relentless focus on fixing potholes, improving school administration, managing municipal budgets efficiently, and being accessible to constituent concerns—boring governance competence is the best electoral insurance in this demographic.",
          "Avoid positioning school or municipal governance issues as partisan culture-war proxies: in a district this educated and prosperous, framing school board conflicts or municipal budget disputes through a partisan lens actively alienates the swing voters most likely to determine the outcome—who are evaluating on substance and competence, not ideological purity."
