          "Engage Hispanic/Latino and Asian communities with specific constituent attention and culturally informed economic messaging — at 12.52% and 6.8% respectively, these communities are large enough to be decisive in a 60-40 seat but can become invisible in generic renter-focused framing; their workforce, small-business, and family economic concerns deserve particularized attention.",
          "Understand the 40% opposition as economically driven, not ideological — at 40% in a Democratic state district, the opposition likely reflects homeowners or older voters concerned about taxes and service delivery, not a cohesive ideological alternative; holding the seat requires preventing defection among persuadable moderate homeowners while consolidating renter support.",
