          "Build specific engagement with the 22.18% Hispanic/Latino constituency around labor standards, wage theft enforcement, and workplace safety — these are the concrete economic justice concerns of a growing demographic group that can determine electoral margins in a 56-44 district if mobilized or neglected.",
          "Address the 25.4% college attainment rate and constrained economic mobility directly: job quality, wage progression pathways, and affordable healthcare access are more salient to a working-class constituency than abstract progressive positioning — offer specific legislative remedies tied to their economic constraints.",
          "Defend against the 44% opposition by understanding whether it is concentrated among older homeowners, white working-class voters with different economic priorities, or both — and offer concrete economic security messaging that distinguishes the Democratic offer rather than assuming renter and Hispanic loyalty."
