          { name: "Young District Economic Mobility & Cost of Living", tag: "lean-into", why: "At 32.8 years median age, CT-HD-84 is a younger constituency where economic opportunity and affordability directly drive voter behavior and satisfaction. The combination of 65% renters, $49,429 income, and only 15.6% college attainment suggests a working-class community where housing costs, childcare, healthcare expenses, and wage growth are the primary economic security concerns. A legislative agenda built around renter protections, affordable housing development, living wage standards, and accessible healthcare — not abstract economic positioning — reflects what this demographic majority actually evaluates on." },
          { name: "Unopposed 2024 Result as Vulnerability Signal", tag: "careful", why: "Santiago's unopposed 2024 victory (100% Dem, 0% Rep) could reflect either durable constituent satisfaction or insufficient Republican investment in a district Republicans wrote off as unwinnable. The district's 55% Hispanic, 13% Black, 30% white composition and younger median age suggest demographics that lean Democratic, but the 65% renter rate, low college attainment, and $49k income mean this constituency has material economic concerns that respond to credible problem-solving regardless of partisan label. A challenger with authentic engagement on cost-of-living issues and demonstrated capacity to deliver could activate suppressed opposition; Santiago's incumbency advantage is real but not guaranteed against a well-resourced, locally credible challenger who speaks to economic anxiety." },
          { name: "Treating Unopposed Victory as Permanent Coalition", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed 2024 result does not indicate a permanently consolidated electorate — it indicates an absence of credible opposition, which is strategically different. In a district where 65% of households rent, median income is below $50k, and the demographic majority is working-class Hispanic/Latino and Black residents, economic anxiety is present whether or not it has been electorally mobilized. A representative who campaigns as though the unopposed margin signals durable support and neglects to actively demonstrate problem-solving on cost of living, housing, and healthcare will discover that suppressed opposition can be activated by a credible challenger." },
          { name: "Race-Based Coalition Management Without Economic Substance", tag: "avoid", why: "A district that is 55% Hispanic/Latino, 13% Black, and 30% white could tempt a representative into demographic-identity-based campaign strategy — cultural events, language accessibility, group-specific messaging — without substantive engagement on the material economic issues that drive voting behavior. With 65% renter rate and $49,429 income, this constituency evaluates on whether government is delivering tangible relief on housing costs, healthcare access, and wage stability, not whether campaign materials reflect their demographic presence. Any campaign that leads on cultural representation without backing it with specific economic policy proposals will underperform against a challenger who offers concrete answers to cost-of-living concerns." }
