          "Address the working-age, non-college-educated constituency (72.8%) on wage adequacy, job training, and sector-specific economic opportunity — service, retail, and trade workers dominate this district, and legislation on minimum wage, apprenticeship pathways, and employer accountability directly affects constituent household economics.",
