          "Engage the college-educated swing vote on policy substance: with 44.1% college-educated, this district evaluates candidates on expertise and evidence-based answers, not partisan positioning. Demonstrate command of education funding, infrastructure needs, and local governance challenges with the analytical depth this constituency expects.",
          "Integrate minority communities into the affluent suburban narrative: the growing Hispanic (8.72%), Asian (2.95%), and Black (2.84%) populations require authentic inclusion in the quality-of-life framework the district offers — schools, infrastructure, economic opportunity — rather than token acknowledgment or separate community strategies.",
          "Recognize this seat as genuinely competitive: a 52-48 margin is not a majority, it is a contested plurality. Any candidate who campaigns as though their coalition is locked in place, rather than actively engaging the 48% opposition and the persuadable swing voters within the affluent, educated majority, is strategically vulnerable to a credible challenger."
