          "Engage the renter minority and younger professionals with specific economic policy: the 12.7% renter rate represents roughly 12% of the district population whose housing costs, wage growth, and professional opportunity are distinct from the homeowner majority; a candidate who speaks to both constituencies simultaneously is building durability in a 56-44 seat.",
          "Build credential on education quality and funding: with 75.4% college attainment, this is a district where educational institutions, school system performance, and state higher education funding are direct quality-of-life issues with real consequence for property values and professional mobility—position on these issues is more consequential than partisan education-policy rhetoric.",
          "Avoid cultural-identity messaging as a primary strategy: this is a college-educated, professionally-employed, high-income constituency that evaluates on governance competence and alignment with material interests, not cultural positioning or ideological activation—candidates who lead with identity or cultural issues rather than fiscal management and professional-class economic security will find this district's affluent professionals responsive to the opposition."
