          { name: "Abstract 'Law and Order' Framing in a Majority-Minority District", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district that is 70.61% people of color and has the lived experience of racialized policing, criminal justice, and systemic inequity, abstract tough-on-crime messaging without acknowledging police accountability, racial bias in enforcement, and the collateral damage of mass incarceration reads as tone-deaf at best and hostile at worst. The 78% Democratic margin reflects constituent preference for public safety approaches that include both crime reduction and racial justice — not one or the other. Any candidate who deploys generic conservative 'tough on crime' rhetoric without acknowledging the specific history and ongoing reality of racialized justice in communities of color will find that rhetoric actively mobilizing opposition rather than consolidating support." }
