          "Treat the 66% result as a mandate to perform, not permission to coast; in a district with this much education and engagement, constituent contact, policy responsiveness, and local governance competence are the currency of re-election, and any incumbent who assumes the margin is durable without active maintenance will discover it erodes faster than expected."
