          "Recognize the demographic homogeneity as a potential vulnerability: with 78.63% white and 77.5% college-educated, the district offers limited opportunity for coalition-building outside the professional-class base; any credible challenger who can argue that Democratic policies have not delivered measurable results for this specific constituency can erode support more easily than in a more diverse district where coalition breadth provides resilience."
