          { name: "Taking the Minority Coalition for Granted or Providing Symbolic Acknowledgment Without Service Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "Latino, Black, and Asian communities are 50% of the district and their support is conditional on whether they experience responsive constituent service and policy delivery on their economic concerns — not on rhetorical appeals or diversity gestures. If these communities perceive the incumbent as inattentive, slow to respond to constituent complaints, or not delivering on economic mobility and healthcare access issues, they have both the electoral power and the political sophistication to withdraw support, decline turnout, or support a primary challenger with a more responsive profile." }
