          { name: "Ignoring the Homeowner Majority's Fixed-Cost Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "With 71.6% homeownership and 41.1 median age, CT-SD-19 is a constituency of homeowners with significant asset exposure and real vulnerability to property tax increases, insurance cost spikes, and whether local government is efficiently managing fixed costs; messaging that does not directly address these material household concerns misses the central evaluative framework of the district's dominant constituency. A candidate who does not speak with specificity and credibility on property tax policy and fiscal management is ceding the economic narrative to the opposition." }
