          "For the challenger: consolidate the affluent homeowner base on fiscal conservatism and regulatory burden; the 43% Republican foundation is entirely recoverable if messaging frames Democratic governance as economically costly and Republican governance as delivering the same quality of life at lower tax burden.",
          "Engage Hispanic and Asian communities with specificity on economic opportunity and business environment; these communities are not monolithic Democratic constituencies—they evaluate on whether government is expanding or constraining economic mobility, and messaging on this dimension can shift material vote share.",
          "Recognize that 57% is not a supermajority—it is a working coalition of affluent professionals who evaluate on performance, not partisan identity; any candidate who treats this as a safe seat and shifts focus away from constituent delivery will find the margin rapidly eroded in a rematch cycle."
